<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Gorgonne Diaspora Cabals

''The serpent-folk of the sea-roads'', scattered across the harbors and skyjammer decks of many
Nexuses — a diaspora organized as cabals, crews, and great-houses rather than any homeland. The
heritage rides the Plane-Touched Gorgonne line: hair-serpents as spirit-familiars, the clans'
discounted //Serpent's Gaze//, and the old appearance canon that already named them at sea —
''"captains with serpents for braids."''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/appearance>>

!! Appearance Canon

The sea-going cabals descend the ''Euryale line — "the far-roaming"'' — a sailor's lineage by
its own name. The type: the ''beautiful-Medusa'' face of the later tellings, ''serpent braids
dressed with coin-rings'' (a crew's shared purse rides in its captain's hair), ''small bronze
wing-vestiges at the temples'' — the archaic wings and bronze hands surviving as ornament-scale
inheritance — and ''smoked-glass gaze-spectacles'' worn as courtesy and couture both.

''The spectacle weld:'' gorgonne gaze-courtesy invented the fashion the harbor guilds now wear
as status — the "Ray-Bane Navigators" of the Third Oar descend from gorgonne courtesy-glass.
Wearing smoked lenses around a gorgonne reads as good manners; refusing them reads as either
deep trust or a challenge, and every gorgonne knows which before you do.

''Shipboard culture:'' mirror-taboos run the decks — polished metal stays below, sightlines get
rigged with cloth, and a crew's toasts run in rounds, in sequence, by rank.

<<~/ahu>>

